    "prologue": "<p>One argument has swallowed an unreasonable amount of oxygen: either accept every page of a large collection as the work of one author, or admit that you have rejected the tenth Guru. That is a demand for allegiance disguised as a question about books. A manuscript cannot be dated by measuring the loyalty of the person looking at it.</p><p>I want to separate three questions. Who composed a particular work? How was it collected and transmitted? What authority does a community give it? The answers can overlap, but they are not interchangeable. A prayer can have an established place in worship while scholars debate the history of the collection in which it appears. A work can be old without being the Guru Granth Sahib. A character can speak inside a story without the author commanding the reader to imitate that character.</p><p>The Dasam Granth is associated with Guru Gobind Singh Ji and contains different kinds of writing. Debate over authorship and compilation is real. This chapter does not pretend to resolve every manuscript problem. It shows why the loudest shortcuts do not resolve them either. The standard throughout is specific: name the composition, the witness, the passage and the question. A whole book cannot be checked through one cropped line. <a class=\"w-cite\" href=\"https://giss.org/pdf/GGS.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"Gurinder Singh Mann, Sources for the Study of Guru Gobind Singh's Life and Times, Journal of Punjab Studies 15 (2008), pp. 229-284\">[Source 1]</a></p><p class=\"w-signature\">Lovepreet Singh · MisterLove</p><blockquote class=\"w-pullquote\"><p>Truthful living gives truth a place in conduct.</p><cite>Author's explanatory paraphrase of the emphasis on truthful conduct, Siri Raag, Guru Nanak Dev Ji, ang 62. <a class=\"w-cite\" href=\"https://www.srigranth.org/servlet/gurbani.gurbani?Action=Page&amp;Param=62\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" aria-label=\"Sri Guru Granth Sahib Ji, Siri Raag, Guru Nanak Dev Ji, ang 62\">[Source 2]</a></cite></blockquote>",
